NativeXRenderer: skip a device call that arrives without a device.

The call table marks a call's first argument as the D3D device ("dev") and
the state tracker reads device state through it. A hook mapped to such a
call that is really another function can pass no device at all: the game's
device factory at 0x82DB11C0 ignores r3 and its callers pass 0 (Sonic
Generations maps it to SetShaderGPRAllocation). The tracker then reads
device state at guest address 0 and crashes the game.

Skip such calls with one warning naming the hook instead: a call without a
device cannot be tracked, and it is not draw state. The submodule stays
pristine: this patch is applied to its working tree at build time
(android/build.sh, ios/build.sh), like native_x_renderer-android-window.patch.

diff --git a/src/state.cpp b/src/state.cpp
index d795b50..d5f89a3 100644
--- a/src/state.cpp
+++ b/src/state.cpp
@@ -295,6 +295,19 @@ void StateTracker::Enter(Call call, uint32_t device, const uint8_t* base, bool n
     return;
   }
   bool device_call = Info(call).device;
+  // A call the table says carries the D3D device in r3, called without one: the hook is mapped to a
+  // function with other arguments (Sonic Generations maps its device factory at 0x82DB11C0 to
+  // SetShaderGPRAllocation; the factory ignores r3 and its callers pass 0). Tracking would read device
+  // state at guest address 0 and crash the game, so skip such calls (the one warning names the hook).
+  if (device_call && device == 0) {
+    static bool warned = false;
+    if (!warned) {
+      warned = true;
+      REXLOG_WARN("[native_x_renderer] {} was called without a device: mislabeled hook, skipped",
+                  Info(call).name);
+    }
+    return;
+  }
   if (!device_call && !((Info(call).flags & kPackets) && last_device_)) return;
   if (device_call) last_device_ = device;
   device = device_call ? device : last_device_;
